note right
  **REPRODUCIBILITY GAP — three different pinning regimes in one repo.**

  · `orchestrator/requirements.txt:3-28` — every constraint is a **lower bound**
    (`fastapi>=0.115`, `pydantic>=2.7`, `langgraph>=0.2`,
    `openai>=1.50`, `transformers>=4.51`, `lancedb>=0.15`, …).
    **No `==`, no upper bound, no lockfile anywhere in the repo.**
    Two builds a week apart install different majors, with nothing to diff.
    `torch` is deliberately unpinned and inherited from the base image
    (`requirements.txt:2`), so the image is buildable on that base only.
  · `sync-worker/requirements.txt` — **caps majors**
    (`httpx>=0.27,<1`, `PyJWT>=2.8,<3`, `duckdb>=1.0,<2`, `pandas>=2.2,<3`,
    `lancedb>=0.8,<1`). Still no hash lock, but bounded.
  · `frontend/package-lock.json` — **fully locked.** The only
    reproducible build in the repo.
  · Container images use moving tags: `vllm/vllm-openai:nightly`
    (docker-compose.yml:36,156) and `searxng/searxng:latest` (`:337`).
    `README.md:273-276` warns operators **not** to `docker compose pull`
    because a newer nightly "can silently break model loading" — i.e. the
    deployment is reproducible only by never re-pulling.

  `orchestrator/requirements-dev.txt` also omits `python-multipart`, which
  `app/uploads.py:66-71` needs at import time — on a clean host installing
  exactly that file, **12 test files fail at collection**. Latent only
  because this machine happens to have it installed.
end note

note left
  **THE SUITES ARE GOOD; THE PIPELINE IS ABSENT.** 1 141 assertions is
  strong coverage for a system this size, and several tests encode real
  regressions (8-thread SQLite race, lying-central-directory zip bomb,
  background-vs-synchronous compaction race, prompt-injection canaries).

  What no one can see, because nothing runs automatically:
  · **5 tests cannot fail.** `test_search_off.py:9-29` re-implements the
    gate locally and ends `assert True`; `test_search_engine.py:111-116`
    asserts `settings.search_enabled in (True, False)`;
    `test_conversation_integrity.py:553-566` monkeypatches the checker to
    itself; `test_chart_pipeline.py:197-199` is `assert x is None or True`;
    `test_history_v3.py:162-176` posts to a route that 404s.
  · **6 files assert on source strings, not behaviour** — e.g.
    `test_effort_depth.py:126-136` asserts a literal line of Python is
    present. Behaviour-preserving refactors break them; behaviour changes
    that keep the literal do not.
  · **Three flake candidates**: a real TCP connect to `127.0.0.1:9`
    (`test_context_budget.py:168-176`), a fixed `/tmp/many.json` path
    (`test_sf_dictionary.py:82,84`), and 8 OS threads on one SQLite file
    (`test_conversation_integrity.py:431-461`).
  · `orchestrator/.dockerignore:5` excludes `tests/`, so the orchestrator
    suite **cannot run inside the built image** — it is host-only, on a
    different Python minor than the containers actually ship.
end note

